# Slackware-Mini-Quota-HOWTO:
# To really activate quotas, you'll need to add 'usrquota' and/or
# 'grpquota' to the appropriate partitions as listed in /etc/fstab.
# Here's an example:
#
# /dev/hda2      /home      ext3     defaults,usrquota      1   1
#
# You'll then need to setup initial quota files at the top of the
# partitions to support quota, like this:
#
# touch /home/aquota.user /home/aquota.group
# chmod 600 /home/aquota.user /home/aquota.group
#
# Then, uncomment the service below and reboot to activate the system.
#quotaon-all
# To edit user quotas, use 'edquota'. See 'man edquota'. Also, the
# official Quota Mini-HOWTO has lots of useful information. That can be
# found here: /usr/doc/Linux-HOWTOs/Quota
